  "question": "Which costs require fewer mounted nodes, and what selection, find and export guarantees survive partial DOM coverage?",
  "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
  "method": "best-api-review/history-v3",
  "trigger": "The owner asked for a best-api-review audit of every open ledger unit, frozen from status at fe0e9599a6 on 2026-10-04 (39 units), and judged afresh because earlier verdicts came from a weaker model. It asked for verdicts only, so no plan, build or panel follows in this run. This scope was open as deferred at queue position 5. It is not the unit next returned, which was reads.",
  "requirements": [
    "Document size or viewport never silently omits content from ordinary Editable or EditorContent.",
    "DOM omission is an explicit mounted-view choice; it never activates from a threshold or automatic strategy.",
    "Canonical document, history, collaboration and selection stay complete under omission; selected and requested targets stay mounted.",
    "Pagination owns page omission and canvas coordinates without the generic top-level virtualizer.",
    "The optional virtualizer dependency stays out of ordinary React consumers.",
    "Native Find, accessibility traversal and print claims stay service-specific; DOM presence does not prove them."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "This review reused the 2026-09-12 deep-contract lanes, the plan's P0/P4 package comparison and the P1-P3 prototype results as historical evidence. It rechecked the live plitejs/react/virtualized and platejs/react/virtualized exports, the sole @tanstack import, the absence of packages/plitejs/src/react/dom-strategy and of domStrategy/findPolicy, PagedEditable's virtualize boolean over WindowedEditable, and the Plate virtualized guide. It noted the external-text plan's 2026-09-15 report of an unrelated huge-document Chromium selection failure in the strict lane.",
  "summary": "The job is to edit large documents without size-driven DOM loss, while letting an app deliberately bound live DOM with honest native-service limits. Paginated content owns its own page window. The old Defer gated runtime adoption on P0-P4. P0/P4 measured the single-entrypoint flag at 9,011 gzip bytes and 2.96 percent, which selected the dedicated plitejs/react/virtualized and platejs/react/virtualized entrypoints, and P1-P3 passed. Live source matches the target. VirtualizedEditable validates estimatedBlockSize and overscan at its boundary, and only the virtualized entrypoint imports TanStack. The dom-strategy directory, the auto/staged modes and findPolicy are gone, and PagedEditable uses its own page mount plan with a virtualize boolean. The strongest deletion would remove viewport rendering in favor of DOM-present CSS containment. It still loses the explicit bounded-DOM and paginated-window jobs that doctrine names, and no new evidence favors it. The remaining S7 stable-snapshot integration proof verifies the adopted design. It is not a gap that decides the design.",
  "verdict": "stop",
  "previous": "2026-09-12-large-documents-deep-contract",
  "relation": "supersedes",
  "reconciliation": [
    {
      "record": "2026-09-12-large-documents-deep-contract",
      "question": "Which costs require fewer mounted nodes, and what selection, find and export guarantees survive partial DOM coverage?",
      "action": "supersedes",
      "reason": "Its Defer waited on the P0-P4 runtime gates and adoption. Those gates passed and S1-S6 installed the target, so a Stop that keeps the adopted design replaces the Defer. Its native-service limits stay as proof limits."
    }
  ],
  "alternatives": [
    "Keeping the adopted explicit-omission design wins. Every concept row in the deep-contract ledger is installed, and the deferred gates passed.",
    "The frozen P0/P4 bundle comparison rejected a single Editable with a virtualize flag (9,011 gzip bytes, 2.96 percent over both limits).",
    "Deleting viewport rendering and relying on DOM-present CSS containment loses the explicit bounded-DOM and paginated page-window jobs. Containment remains a separate unmeasured experiment, not a substitute.",
    "A model-global virtualization store or extension loses, because two views of one editor can have different coverage and scroll owners.",
    "Routing pagination through the generic virtualizer with normalized public offsets is rejected because it creates a second coordinate system, and the source already cut it."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "This is a source review only. S7 (source-first types, packed consumers, production benchmark with correctness guard, managed cross-browser matrix on one stable snapshot) has not run and stays an open gate in docs/plans/2026-09-11-large-documents-api-review.md. On 2026-09-15 the strict Chromium lane stopped on a huge-document selection assertion that the external-text plan recorded as out of scope. Its current status is unknown here. This review has no native Find, assistive technology, print, physical IME or device proof. docs/vision/plite.md carries an unrelated staged hunk that shifts line numbers by seven.",
